  data:  # d05b
    kind: work_item  # d05b
    title: "swift: a declared-but-UNTYPED name does not shadow -- _type_of falls through it to an outer binding or the field and stamps that type on a different variable; and if/for/do blocks are not scopes"  # d05b
    status: todo_hard  # d05b
    priority: 3  # d05b
    parent:  # d05b
    tags:  # d05b
    - swift  # d05b
    - analysis_quality  # d05b
    isbefore: []  # d05b
    duplicate_of: []  # d05b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d05b
    pr_ref:  # d05b
    description: "FILED 2026-10-01 from WI-mofil-tidog-forob-tovah-givud-lijog-vuvug-gutid's A/B read-back.\n\nMECHANISM. The swift binding pass records a name only when it can TYPE it. A declared-but-untyped name -- an unannotated closure parameter, a local whose initialiser the registry cannot type, a parameter of an unextractable type -- leaves NO entry, so `_type_of` falls THROUGH it to an outer binding, `var_types`, or `_inherited_field_type`, and stamps the OUTER name's type on a different variable. ABSENT != EMPTY: an untyped declaration is a positive claim that shadows, and is read as nothing.\n\nINSTANCES, read back:\n  hummingbird Sources/HummingbirdCore/Request/URI.swift:46-47  `queries.map { query -> ... in var query = query; ... query.read(until:) }` -- the closure parameter `query` is unannotated, so the receiver resolves through the OUTER `guard var query = _query` (Parser). Correct only because both are Parser.\n  fixture (WI-mofil probe): `func go(s: FileManager) { let s = s.makeSession(store); s.dataTask(with: u) }` -- the local s is untyped (no registry row), so `s.dataTask` is stamped FileManager from the parameter it shadows: swift:FileManager:0-0:dataTask.\n\nA second, related gap: an `if`/`for`/`do` body is not a scope in the map (only functions and, since WI-mofil, closures are), so a binding inside one block types a same-named receiver AFTER the block. Pre-existing; WI-mofil made scoped bindings position-aware (visible from the end of the declaration) but not block-scoped.\n\nDIRECTION. Record every declaration in its scope with a None type (a tombstone) and stop the lookup at the innermost visible binding, typed or not; make `statements` blocks scopes (guard binds into its PARENT block, if/while-let into the body). Measure BOTH directions: tombstones REMOVE stamps, some of which are coincidentally correct today (Kingfisher ProcessorCollectionViewController.swift:88 was typed UIAlertController only through a closure-local leak WI-mofil closed)."  # d05b
    fields: {}  # d05b
- op: discuss  # ddf1
  at: '2026-10-04T06:11:24Z'  # ddf1
  by: agent  # ddf1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ddf1
  clock: 2  # ddf1
  nonce: ddf1  # ddf1
  message: "WI-silos worked on branch jgstern-agent/fix/silos (worktree ~/hg_wt/silos, base origin/dev 385ec63be1), commit 41fd9834a6. NOT pushed or merged; status unchanged. Full report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/silos.md (A/B artefacts in run_10032026/silos/).\n\nWHAT: every declaration is recorded in its scope, typed or not (binding = (visible_from, visible_to, type|None)), and the innermost visible binding decides. This covers unannotated closure params, untyped locals, params of unextracted types, for-in vars, catch / case-let / if-case / tuple names. Blocks are scopes (_SWIFT_BLOCK_NODES: statements + if/while/for/catch/switch_entry). An if-clause binding ends at the else; a loop var does not cover its sequence; guard binds the enclosing block; a statements under ERROR is not a scope. Same family, also fixed: protocol_function_declaration params no longer leak file-wide; multi-binding `let a = X(), b = y()` is read per clause. Two exposed typing gaps fixed in the shared walker: initialisers get the field resolver (if let b = self.body), and x! carries x's type. File level (var_types) deliberately untouched (WI-tagir).\n\nTESTS: test_swift_untyped_binding_shadows.py (25). The first 20 ran on dev: 18 failed, 2 passed (the controls). 14 mutation runs, each reds its pinned test. Targeted smart-test on the final tree: 10016 passed, 2 xfailed, 0 failed, changed files at 100% coverage; module_key_axis pins relocated (2216 / 2287).\n\nMEASURED (frozen copies, analyze_swift per call site): calls totals identical; 375 sites changed (vapor 63, hummingbird 37, Kingfisher 48, Alamofire 227), almost all stamp REMOVALS. SLOT 1068->1027 / 816->791 / 912->888 / 489->478. Read-back: removed stamps at untyped LOCALS were right by name coincidence (12/12 sampled), while those at closure params (8/12), params (9/12) and loop vars (4/5) were mostly WRONG. In a random 30, 25 were removals of right stamps (mostly Alamofire tests' stored(Session()) cascade). This is a measured RECALL LOSS, not a precision win, on this corpus. L5: catalogued io unchanged on vapor/hummingbird/Alamofire; Kingfisher total_io_edges 63->60 (3 FileManager fs chains via `let fileManager = config.fileManager`, previously typed through another type's property in the file-level map).\n\nFILED: WI-tagir (file-level var_types pools every type's properties), WI-hojib (untyped initialiser shapes behind the recall loss), WI-sajol (capture-list declarations). Notes posted on WI-sizas, WI-rajig, WI-bodav, WI-zobif, INV-vakar."  # ddf1
