  message: "From WI-hojib + WI-tagir (branch jgstern-agent/fix/hojib, commits on top of 41fd9834a6, not merged). The recall loss measured here, re-measured with silos's method (4 frozen repos, call-site rows, arm A = origin/dev 385ec63be1, S = this branch 41fd9834a6, B = silos+hojib):\n\n- Of the 272 call sites where S asserts less than A (a resolved edge, a filled slot or a hint removed), B restores A's exact rows at 141. Sites: vapor 11/48, hummingbird 4/33, Kingfisher 25/32, Alamofire 101/159. A read of 20 random restored sites found 20 right.\n- At 121 sites B keeps S's rows. A read of 30 random kept sites found:\n  - 13 wrong stamps correctly staying removed;\n  - 11 right stamps still lost, all through closure parameters (WI-zobif), case payloads / tuples (WI-rajig), collection elements (WI-bodav), or closure-result typing;\n  - 6 unclear.\n- At 10 sites B has a third state, read and all right.\n- Kingfisher io-boundaries total_io_edges: 63 (A) -> 60 (S) -> 68 (B). The 3 lost FileManager chains return; 0 catalogued chains are lost on any of the 4 repos.\n\nRecord: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/hojib.md."  # b657
